<!DOCTYPE DM SYSTEM>
<!-- Field-level help for the TSO/E LOGON "Size" field. Shown when the cursor is
     in the Size field and HELP (PF1) is pressed, instead of the panel's general
     help (tsohelp) - DTL <dtafld help="sizehelp">. PF3 returns to the logon panel.
     Auto-flow (ISPDTLC-idiomatic): no row/col; the title centres itself, and the
     conversion utility spaces the paragraphs. -->
<panel name="sizehelp">TSO/E LOGON - Size Field HELP
  <info>
    <p>The <hp>Size</hp> field sets the region size, in kilobytes, for your TSO
       address space - the amount of virtual storage your session may use.</p>

    <p><hp>Rules:</hp></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Numeric only.</li>
      <li>Range 0 to 32768 (a larger value is rejected with message TSO001).</li>
      <li>The default is 00150. Leave it unless your work needs more storage.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Press ENTER or PF3 to return to the LOGON panel and continue.</p>
  </info>

  <botinst>PF3=Return</botinst>

  <keyl name="HELPKEYS">
    <keyi key="PF3"  cmd="EXIT">Return</keyi>
    <keyi key="PF15" cmd="EXIT">Return</keyi>
  </keyl>
</panel>
